From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: allow out-of-tree builds in any directory

README-12-vpath-builds says an out-of-tree build directory must be
below the top-level source directory, at most four levels deep.
configure finds the source directory by searching upwards from the
build directory for configure.ac, at most four times, and otherwise
silently takes the build directory instead; apl --show_src_dir then
prints the wrong directory, and the SVN revision of Archive.cc is not
found.  svnversion is run in the build directory, not the source
directory.  configure also adds -I`pwd`, the absolute build directory,
to the user variable CXXFLAGS, so that configure's output files are
found, which automake already provides with -I$(top_builddir).

Take the source directory from $srcdir, which configure already knows,
run svnversion on it, and drop the -I`pwd`.

README-12-vpath-builds now says that out-of-tree builds work in the
standard way, and no longer describes the directory restrictions, nor
the make VPATH_clean target, which no longer exists.  A source tree
configured in place is rejected by configure, so 'make distclean'
there suffices.

Forwarded: no
---
--- a/README-12-vpath-builds
+++ b/README-12-vpath-builds
